  "cause": "**On Monday the United States bombed an Iranian island, and the first thing every report mentioned was the election.** US officials told **CBS** that strikes hit **Qeshm Island** in the Strait of Hormuz, describing them as **limited** and as a response to the **IRGC firing on a US aircraft**. Iran's state agency **Irna** reported several explosions on Qeshm. The IRGC did not confirm the strikes but said its forces had **shot down two US MQM-170 reconnaissance drones** south of the island and an **MQ-9** east of the strait. The timing is the story: the strikes came **the day before US midterm elections**, in a war that began when the US and Israel attacked Iran in **February**, and with **Trump's polling falling** and his own party pressing him to end it. **The same day, the President described the war as a matter of scheduling.** He told **Axios** he was in **\"no rush\"** to escalate — *\"One way or the other, we will do something, but there is no rush. We crippled them financially… They have no money, no gasoline and their people are getting very tired of it.\"* To **Fox News** on the eve of the vote he said the US **\"might need to go after Pickaxe [Mountain]\"**, the underground site linked to Iran's nuclear programme, adding that it was **\"not a big deal\"** and could be done in **\"one hour\"**. Asked directly whether significant strikes would resume after the midterms, he said **\"no\"**. The **Associated Press**, citing two regional officials, reported that **Netanyahu** had pushed Trump during a weekend call for **another wave of strikes on Iran after the midterms**. **Tehran answered in the conditional, and the mediators kept working.** Iran's chief negotiator, parliament speaker **Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf**, said on Tuesday: *\"The ball is now in America's court to prevent war… Just as the Islamic Republic of Iran stands ready for battle with its finger on the trigger, it has also given the American side a powerful and rational response.\"* Foreign Minister **Abbas Araghchi** told Irna that **\"very intensive\"** talks to end the war were under way with the US through **Qatari and Pakistani** mediators, and that Iran was prepared for both scenarios. A Qatari delegation arrived in Tehran on Monday. The standing offer is the one from last week: **reopen the Strait of Hormuz within two days** once the US meets **seven conditions**, reportedly including **lifting the naval blockade of Iranian ports** and **releasing frozen Iranian assets**. A preliminary agreement to end the war and reopen the strait was reached in **June** and collapsed within weeks. **And the war has already reached the Gulf states that are trying to mediate it.** In October a **Houthi missile attack on Riyadh's airport killed 13 people and wounded more than 300** — and the consequences now arrive as cancellations: the **2027 Asian Cup**, a 24-team tournament due in Saudi Arabia from 7 January, has been **postponed to December 2027–January 2028**, while the **Six Kings Slam** tennis exhibition and the **Asian Tour's** season-ending golf event have been cancelled or indefinitely postponed. Gulf states have warned Iran of **individual and collective retaliation** over attacks on their territory. The **UAE** has said publicly that **military solutions offer no quick off-ramps**; **NYT** reports Gulf governments in a flurry of mediation to avert a war many fear will be worse this time; the **UN** warns that Hormuz and Red Sea disruption is squeezing food supplies; Gulf growth has plunged across the war while US oil industry profit ran at roughly **three times** the 2025 figure for the same months.",
