   "**A limited strike on the eve of a vote is a message to voters delivered to Iranians** — Qeshm bombed on Monday, the polls on Tuesday, \"no rush\" to Axios and \"one hour\" to Fox in the same news cycle; the direct effect is that the strike's military purpose cannot be separated from its domestic one; the compound consequence is that the war's tempo is now indexed to the American electoral calendar, so escalation and pause both arrive on a date that has nothing to do with the conflict — and Tehran reads every quiet week as a polling interval",
   "**\"Not a big deal… one hour\" is a doctrine spoken aloud before it is executed** — Pickaxe Mountain named on television with a duration attached; the direct effect is that the target set is being previewed rather than decided; the compound consequence is that a nuclear-linked facility described as a one-hour item invites the other side to treat *any* strike on it as existential, which is the threshold that removes the space between conventional and unthinkable — and a previewed target is a warned target, so the next attempt meets a prepared defence",
   "**The two-day reopening is being negotiated while the strike aircraft are still flying** — seven conditions, a two-day clock, Qatari and Pakistani mediators, a Qatari delegation in Tehran, and a limited bombing the day before; the direct effect is that the offer is credible enough to discuss and cheap enough to abandon; the compound consequence is the June pattern repeating — agreement, attacks on shipping, blockade reinstated — because the deal on the table prices a *lane*, not the blockade, the frozen assets or the enrichment file, so it has no mechanism that survives its own first violation",
