  "verse": "Do not allow yourselves to foment chaos in the land and amongst the people… and as you shall bind yourselves to the truth, so you shall not kill, neither your enemies nor your sons and daughters, just as you as man and woman shall not kill one another; Gewalt is given to you over life and death so that you may protect life and prevent death… because truly you shall not kill people of your kind (human beings) but rather save yourselves from death and Gewalt (terror).",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 7, Verse 127",
  "hinge": "The cause is not the drone and it is not the truce. It is the choice — by Moscow, whether a pause is a concession granted to a patron or a practice it can extend; by Kyiv, whether the Abu Dhabi talks open with the dead or with the architecture; by both ombudsmen, whether their joint inspection becomes an institution with a ledger or a photograph; and by the states supplying interceptors, whether the answer to a fifth refinery strike and a 29-death aid centre is a production line or a communiqué. §7:127 gives force exactly one licence — to protect life — and everything done with it beyond that is the chaos the verse names first."
