  "cause": "**The arithmetic has not moved, and the two men who need it are now formally competing for it.** **Benjamin Netanyahu** and **Gadi Eisenkot** each presented their case to **President Isaac Herzog** for the first chance to build a coalition, after the Central Elections Committee certified a result with no majority in it: **Likud and its allies 53** seats, **Eisenkot's bloc 48**, and the two **Arab-led parties a record 19** — on the **highest turnout in nearly three decades**. Neither bloc can reach 61 without those 19 seats. Both can reach 61 with them. Neither has said it will. **What has changed is that the obstacle is now described as a principle.** **NYT** reports that Arab lawmakers give Netanyahu's opponents a **clear majority** in the Knesset — and that **many Jewish lawmakers are trying to avoid relying on them**. Relatives of **7 October** victims have publicly called on opposition leaders to form a **\"government of change\"**, which is a demand that the 19 seats be used rather than feared. **NPR** describes the campaign that produced 53 seats as **\"Netanyahu's fear campaign\"**, which won \"a large share of support\" in an inconclusive election. Likud, having lost its majority, alleges **foreign interference** and says the Arab-led parties **\"stole\"** the election — a claim for which no evidence has been published. The opposition says Netanyahu is trying to **\"delegitimise\"** the vote. Herzog, who has urged parties to engage \"with an open heart\" to avoid a fresh election, must issue a mandate of up to **42 days**, and analysts still rate another election the likeliest outcome. **Underneath the certificate, the file the next government inherits keeps being added to.** Israeli strikes in **Gaza** killed at least **eight** people on Sunday and Monday, including a **four-year-old boy** — three beside **Cairo School** in Gaza City's al-Rimal, and **five Hamas-run police officers** aged 23 to 53 in **al-Mawasi** near Khan Younis. The military said it struck \"military operatives\" and published no evidence. A ceasefire has been in force since **October last year**; **1,580** people have been killed since it began, per Gaza's health ministry, whose figures the UN considers reliable; **74,594** have been killed since the war started. The Trump-brokered peace plan has stalled.",
  "bullets": [
   "**A majority that exists arithmetically and is refused politically has one destination: another election** — 53, 48, 19, and a 42-day mandate that cannot produce 61 without a bloc both sides treat as unmentionable; the direct effect is that Herzog's mandate becomes a procedure for demonstrating impossibility; the compound consequence is that a third election in two years is fought on the same arithmetic and the same refusal, and each repetition makes the refusal look more like a fact of nature than a decision",
   "**\"Many Jewish lawmakers are trying to avoid relying on them\" is the crisis stated politely** — a clear majority exists and the people who hold it are being managed around; the direct effect is that 19 certified seats are treated as a constraint rather than a component; the compound consequence is that a fifth of the electorate is permanently positioned outside the possible, so the state's coalition mathematics and its citizenship have come apart — and no budget passes twice on that basis",
   "**Calling the count stolen makes the next count the only appeal** — \"foreign interference\", \"stole the election\", nothing published, in a country whose adversaries need no help doubting its legitimacy; the direct effect is that the result must be defended rather than used; the compound consequence is that the accusation is available to every future loser at every level, and a democracy whose results are contestable by assertion has moved sovereignty from the ballot to the studio",
   "**The relatives of 7 October are asking for the opposite of what the campaign promised** — a \"government of change\" from the people with the strongest standing to demand anything; the direct effect is that the security and hostage file now has a constituency pressing for a coalition rather than an election; the compound consequence is that if the call fails, those families become the permanent evidence that the system could not be moved by the people it most wronged — and that disillusionment outlasts every government",
   "**A caretaker with a stalled plan and a rising baseline leaves the next government a floor it cannot lower** — 1,580 dead inside a ceasefire, eight more this weekend, \"military operatives\" published without evidence, 74,594 since the war began; the direct effect is that violations cost nothing because nobody is empowered to price them; the compound consequence is that each week of deadlock adds to a toll inherited as normal, and normality is the one thing in politics no election can reverse",
   "**The hinge is whether a candidate says the sentence that makes 61 possible, and whether the campaign's central claim is evidenced or withdrawn** — the moment someone states plainly that a coalition resting on Arab-led parties is legitimate, which is a political choice and not a moral one; the moment \"stole the election\" is documented or retracted; the moment Herzog's 42 days are used to publish each bloc's price rather than to run down the clock; and the moment the Gaza ceasefire gets a monitor and a violation ledger instead of a stall. §9:88 addresses this deadlock exactly: do not quarrel with people of your kind because they are not of the same opinion, and do not quarrel about goods and riches — because the quarrel is what is being chosen, by people who could stop choosing it."
  ],
  "verse": "And do not quarrel with one another as people of your kind (human beings) because you are not of the same opinion, and do not quarrel about your goods or about your riches, because only goodness shall be granted to you as people of your kind (human beings) so that it may go well with you.",
